body:
Some men's fragrances become classics because they work almost everywhere: the office, a dinner, a wedding. These are the designer scents our customers ask about most, with the GK version of each and when to wear it.

## For the office and every day

Eventus is our take on Creed Aventus — pineapple, bergamot and birch smoke over oakmoss. Imagine, inspired by Louis Vuitton Imagination, is lighter: citron, neroli and black tea that suits a suit.

{{scents: eventus, imagine}}

## For evenings and cold weather

Midnight Elixir, inspired by Dior Sauvage Elixir, is spicy and warm with lavender, liquorice and amber. Royal Oud, inspired by Tom Ford Oud Wood, is smoky oud and sandalwood — rich without being heavy.

{{scents: midnight-elixir, royal-oud}}

## Something different

King's Code, inspired by Dolce & Gabbana K, opens with cardamom and ginger and dries down to leather and woods. It's bold, and it lasts.

{{scents: kings-code}}
